<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Starkenburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Starkenburg was the southern province of the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and the People's State of Hesse from 1803 to 1937, lying east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> between the Main and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> as its seat. It took its name from Starkenburg castle above Heppenheim, and its lands included much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odenwald">Odenwald</a> and the Bergstraße.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/starkenburg.jpg" alt="Starkenburg" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Störfix on de.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hessen1930.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
